    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// 6/8 against 3/4 (docs/plan/prompts/75)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The other shape polymeter takes, and the cheaper one: the bars are the same" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// *length*, so the barlines never diverge and the whole difference is where" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the beams fall — two dotted quarters against three quarters. *America* is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// this, and so is most of what a Latin American ensemble does with a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// sesquiáltera." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// It is worth having both fixtures because the two shapes cost different" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// things. This one needs no per-staff barline grid at all: one grid, two" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// beamings. `bulgarian.musa` is the one that needs the grid, and the reason" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `bars` takes a scope." },
